    "Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples have lived in Australia for at least 65,000 years: theirs is one of the oldest living cultures in the world. They had hundreds of languages and a deep spiritual relationship with the land, as at Uluru, a sacred red rock in the middle of the country.",
    "In 1770, Captain James Cook claimed the east coast for Britain. On 26 January 1788, the First Fleet arrived in Sydney with about 750 convicts: Britain used Australia as a giant prison. Until 1868, more than 160,000 convicts were sent there. The British considered the land as \"terra nullius\", land belonging to nobody.",
    "For the Aboriginal people, colonisation was a catastrophe: they lost their lands and many died from diseases and violence. From about 1910 to the 1970s, the government took thousands of Aboriginal children from their families to raise them in institutions or white families. They are called the \"Stolen Generations\".",
    "In 1992, the High Court recognised that Aboriginal people had owned the land before 1788. On 13 February 2008, Prime Minister Kevin Rudd officially apologised to the Stolen Generations in Parliament. But inequalities remain, and in 2023 a majority of Australians rejected a proposal to give Indigenous people a special \"Voice\" to Parliament.",
